---
// The assistants hub: every AI assistant a business's inbox works with, and what each needs.
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { ASSISTANTS, CHECKED } from "../../lib/assistants";

const url = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site).toString();
const ld = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "CollectionPage",
  name: "Your business in every AI assistant",
  url,
  hasPart: ASSISTANTS.map((a) => ({
    "@type": "TechArticle",
    headline: a.heading,
    url: new URL(`/assistants/${a.slug}/`, Astro.site).toString(),
  })),
};
---

<Layout
  title="Your business in Meta Muse, Grok, ChatGPT, Claude and Gemini · Surfing Dog"
  description="One inbox every AI assistant can book, quote and order through: Meta Muse, Grok and Grok Bot, ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Copilot Studio. What each needs, and how to connect your own AI."
  image="/art/og-assistant-hub-v1.png"
  ld={ld}
>
  <section class="wrap wrap-read section is-head" aria-labelledby="hub-h">
    <p class="eyebrow">Assistants</p>
    <h1 class="h-page" id="hub-h">Your business in every AI assistant</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      People now ask Meta Muse, Grok, ChatGPT, Claude or Gemini to book the service, get the quote, place the order.
      Each of them speaks MCP, and your inbox answers all of them the same way: in your name, by your rules, with a state
      you can see.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tight" aria-label="Assistants">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ul class="grid-cards" data-reveal="stagger">
        {
          ASSISTANTS.map((a) => (
            <li class="glass card">
              <h2 class="h-card">
                <a class="link" href={`/assistants/${a.slug}/`}>
                  {a.name}
                </a>
              </h2>
              <p class="card-text">{a.lede}</p>
              <p class="card-text muted">{a.plans}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap wrap-read section" aria-labelledby="same-h">
    <h2 class="h-section" id="same-h">What every assistant gets</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>For a customer's assistant</strong>, your public MCP server at <code>/mcp</code>: your services and free
        times, a booking, a quote request, an order, a message, and its answers to what you propose. No sign-in.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>For your own AI</strong>, the owner MCP server at <code>/mcp/owner</code>, with OAuth 2.1 (the assistant
        registers itself) or an owner API key in a header.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The same rules for everyone.</strong> A priced booking or order binds nobody until the person confirmed its
        summary. Your rules decide what is confirmed without you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Every MCP revision</strong> from March 2025 to 2026-07-28, so older and newer assistants both connect.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Found through the network.</strong> Assistants search <code>https://network.surfingdog.ai/mcp</code> for
        verified businesses; see <a class="link" href="/network/">the network</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">Checked {CHECKED} against each assistant's own documentation, linked on its page.</p>
    <p>
      New to this? Start with <a class="link" href="/blog/what-ai-assistants-need-from-your-business/">what a personal AI
      assistant needs from your business</a>.
    </p>
    <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/try/">Try it with the demo shop</a></p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .copy {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--sp-2);
    margin: var(--sp-3) 0 0;
    padding: var(--sp-2) var(--sp-3);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-control);
    background: var(--row-bg);
    font-size: var(--fs-mono);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .muted {
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .prose-steps {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--sp-2);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  .wrap-read.section p + p,
  .wrap-read.section ul + p {
    margin-top: var(--sp-3);
  }
</style>
